    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<div style="background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:5px solid #f7931a;border-radius:8px;padding:18px 22px;margin-bottom:16px;">
<p style="color:#9a3412;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 8px;">S1 Q1 — Gas metering</p>
<p style="color:#1e293b;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;margin:0;">Ethereum charges gas for every instruction and halts a program the instant it runs out. Model that meter.</p>
</div>
<p style="font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;">Write <strong><code>gas_remaining(gas_limit, costs)</code></strong> where <code>gas_limit</code> is an integer and <code>costs</code> is a list of instruction costs, executed in order. Subtract each cost in turn. If at some point the gas left is smaller than the next instruction's cost, stop and return the string <code>"out of gas"</code>. If every instruction runs, return the integer amount of gas remaining.</p>]]></text>
